{"type":"message","id":"dc5ca56a","parentId":"bc095896","timestamp":"2026-03-31T17:17:23.233Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering script fallback options**\n\nI'm thinking about editing the script to possibly use a minimal local request solution. Maybe I can utilize `urllib` while keeping the same interface name? I could also consider trying to import `requests`, and if it fails, define a tiny class with a `post()` method that returns an object containing properties like `status_code`, `text`, `json`, and `url`. That approach seems acceptable and maintains the `requests.post` API call structure. I definitely need to make that edit!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0afe10540796cbee0169cc0191d1548191bf7e408eb6ce309e\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpzAGUGGqBiGkfks3WL8q2o1WhkR1ZumN4qpJirMhHXmeVGfvI9O8JwJz_EXZBJFPoR2QESqIo0aSAyNdrlYiml91iZ65xPgwUdczNZ1WNrSDmxqzRs2h3Y2ox2Uy0KmJPzLG-buwtzy5OeinMYSpr_wwa_VTyAskA39hFn1Bh8AWXPoIm0yIOHOWPjywEUm1Z9LiM6I7EjTbLBOHE8zppdLO6QXVnKHel50DGlk6LAtNgS1e3hUTb2635LT6EN3Ts-uiq4YsFKzdP51bgtpIFuXe_C5DZL6s2hb1u-2tDmJdQwabYTbARS4eOMozy4mDPQX2usZR7y2NXXM74zQo6sYS0UDtGxiclPFbRIXqEl8NXb3ZfV0yYmBmPNEzW1AGxn3F_JY3QhrDD545Vk6egvp8WIKp8UgWO_FEe-mJgvcDBqwBt2NPbeiNGV7T2ZAsoQ1YsZAhuYJV7PrdlmIqGyp6f6pwGeM17CtJPqOmCrPEA_ORFsLwK4eJmhGpsIOm0ncZtXeiA3n9b-jUptRWcns68-2cYDPaO4qObyfoC67Ko4FJv37Sv6_7jsLoBxd6sXWDj7FSLWvErp7LquS3ZUSV6aWbMm_nZKs0fflRBdGnsDLY4IHIVbuaEQHc-0J2RZk-6rBHy1txoswEYMZ7sX0_Q36W0q4W8cbCJHCCRjdy8liFuEtUhrJZEtL-PInBPyxx8QXrJ3AB-8mgqtqA51BUFJwM0sG_v-ECQn_3jFiNAZlEFDi_Zbla81FBku8g1uwpjIULsuoGW0d7T4ejQz1nKYl0v1NMWd7T2sMzHkZLsDs-C0CFqVCHwbtkXX8YE9Kt1_6WZ8njDMFQG6h0Bp4F-41-fak4dwGfeUCJzPtJCtDtHA4WYwMlwWTWFNtUvbJTbDuyWMy5gGOO3kmGNxYZ3T7ioe6iHjFolknRUA6kgtuHM18p9Ci-XylGgdHefpIgGlgMEZvgIWPEtXoATHBp1GXMj02TVBBFUbwuVCl3BS2DatWdiAQYnNoGMITcCjil4MowqZMw7ZPmqEysWoYB7GJvxB6-jlYGgfxaTSf0tvaBTk1nhn3dBtijViAsjlv0NgRwdEfiewWOtDHZQBLEZ-W4LfTNUT-ZGjLhQ8SV5avOpuwQCXUj3wTZ_3r007ToLDVcmk_qzi3BZstIwvfi-LjicPB7_Jo_ZqsvUJcaCl4w8wTYZkRTb5UWkX6WFSYTorZRVwSi33dxHlg2yHA4Tmg==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering script fallback options**\\n\\nI'm thinking about editing the script to possibly use a minimal local request solution. Maybe I can utilize `urllib` while keeping the same interface name? I could also consider trying to import `requests`, and if it fails, define a tiny class with a `post()` method that returns an object containing properties like `status_code`, `text`, `json`, and `url`. That approach seems acceptable and maintains the `requests.post` API call structure. I definitely need to make that edit!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"`pip` also isn’t available here, so I’m adding a small built-in fallback that preserves the same `requests.post(..., params=..., files=...)` call shape when the `requests` package is missing, then I’ll rerun the test.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0afe10540796cbee0169cc019489d48191876351f1a228bd48\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9SFiH58qrppMAa2kHJID6TPk|fc_0afe10540796cbee0169cc01949db481919ba311f63d9eb47e","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/skin-cancer-pipeline/scripts/pipeline_execution_tool.py","old_string":"from pathlib import Path\nfrom urllib import error, request\n\nimport requests\n","new_string":"from pathlib import Path\nfrom urllib import error, parse, request\n\ntry:\n    import requests  # type: ignore\nexcept ImportError:\n    import mimetypes\n    import uuid\n\n    class _FallbackResponse:\n        def __init__(self, url: str, status_code: int, text: str):\n            self.url = url\n            self.status_code = status_code\n            self.text = text\n            self.ok = 200 <= status_code < 300\n\n        def json(self):\n            return json.loads(self.text)\n\n    class _FallbackRequestsException(Exception):\n        pass\n\n    class _FallbackRequestsModule:\n        RequestException = _FallbackRequestsException\n\n        @staticmethod\n        def post(url, params=None, files=None, timeout=None):\n            params = params or {}\n            encoded_query = parse.urlencode(params)\n            final_url = f\"{url}?{encoded_query}\" if encoded_query else url\n\n            boundary = f\"----OpenClawBoundary{uuid.uuid4().hex}\"\n            parts = []\n            for field_name, handle in files or []:\n                file_name = Path(getattr(handle, \"name\", \"upload.bin\")).name\n                mime_type = mimetypes.guess_type(file_name)[0] or \"application/octet-stream\"\n                file_bytes = handle.read()\n                parts.extend(\n                    [\n                        f\"--{boundary}\\r\\n\".encode(\"utf-8\"),\n                        (\n                            f'Content-Disposition: form-data; name=\"{field_name}\"; '\n                            f'filename=\"{file_name}\"\\r\\n'\n                        ).encode(\"utf-8\"),\n                        f\"Content-Type: {mime_type}\\r\\n\\r\\n\".encode(\"utf-8\"),\n                        file_bytes,\n                        b\"\\r\\n\",\n                    ]\n                )\n            parts.append(f\"--{boundary}--\\r\\n\".encode(\"utf-8\"))\n            body = b\"\".join(parts)\n\n            req = request.Request(\n                final_url,\n                data=body,\n                headers={\n                    \"Content-Type\": f\"multipart/form-data; boundary={boundary}\",\n                    \"Accept\": \"application/json\",\n                },\n                method=\"POST\",\n            )\n            try:\n                with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\n                    response_text = resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n                    return _FallbackResponse(final_url, resp.status, response_text)\n            except error.HTTPError as e:\n                response_text = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n                return _FallbackResponse(final_url, e.code, response_text)\n            except Exception as e:\n                raise _FallbackRequestsException(str(e)) from e\n\n    requests = _FallbackRequestsModule()\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/skin-cancer-pipeline/scripts/pipeline_execution_tool.py\",\"old_string\":\"from pathlib import Path\\nfrom urllib import error, request\\n\\nimport requests\\n\",\"new_string\":\"from pathlib import Path\\nfrom urllib import error, parse, request\\n\\ntry:\\n    import requests  # type: ignore\\nexcept ImportError:\\n    import mimetypes\\n    import uuid\\n\\n    class _FallbackResponse:\\n        def __init__(self, url: str, status_code: int, text: str):\\n            self.url = url\\n            self.status_code = status_code\\n            self.text = text\\n            self.ok = 200 <= status_code < 300\\n\\n        def json(self):\\n            return json.loads(self.text)\\n\\n    class _FallbackRequestsException(Exception):\\n        pass\\n\\n    class _FallbackRequestsModule:\\n        RequestException = _FallbackRequestsException\\n\\n        @staticmethod\\n        def post(url, params=None, files=None, timeout=None):\\n            params = params or {}\\n            encoded_query = parse.urlencode(params)\\n            final_url = f\\\"{url}?{encoded_query}\\\" if encoded_query else url\\n\\n            boundary = f\\\"----OpenClawBoundary{uuid.uuid4().hex}\\\"\\n            parts = []\\n            for field_name, handle in files or []:\\n                file_name = Path(getattr(handle, \\\"name\\\", \\\"upload.bin\\\")).name\\n                mime_type = mimetypes.guess_type(file_name)[0] or \\\"application/octet-stream\\\"\\n                file_bytes = handle.read()\\n                parts.extend(\\n                    [\\n                        f\\\"--{boundary}\\\\r\\\\n\\\".encode(\\\"utf-8\\\"),\\n                        (\\n                            f'Content-Disposition: form-data; name=\\\"{field_name}\\\"; '\\n                            f'filename=\\\"{file_name}\\\"\\\\r\\\\n'\\n                        ).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\"),\\n                        f\\\"Content-Type: {mime_type}\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\".encode(\\\"utf-8\\\"),\\n                        file_bytes,\\n                        b\\\"\\\\r\\\\n\\\",\\n                    ]\\n                )\\n            parts.append(f\\\"--{boundary}--\\\\r\\\\n\\\".encode(\\\"utf-8\\\"))\\n            body = b\\\"\\\".join(parts)\\n\\n            req = request.Request(\\n                final_url,\\n                data=body,\\n                headers={\\n                    \\\"Content-Type\\\": f\\\"multipart/form-data; boundary={boundary}\\\",\\n                    \\\"Accept\\\": \\\"application/json\\\",\\n                },\\n                method=\\\"POST\\\",\\n            )\\n            try:\\n                with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\\n                    response_text = resp.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n                    return _FallbackResponse(final_url, resp.status, response_text)\\n            except error.HTTPError as e:\\n                response_text = e.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n                return _FallbackResponse(final_url, e.code, response_text)\\n            except Exception as e:\\n                raise _FallbackRequestsException(str(e)) from e\\n\\n    requests = _FallbackRequestsModule()\\n\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":276,"output":830,"cacheRead":31360,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":32466,"cost":{"input":0.0006900000000000001,"output":0.012450000000000001,"cacheRead":0.00784,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02098}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774977424411}}
